# Declared non-bindings: a repository that deliberately does not bind a shimmed
# hook, with the reason.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS.
#
# Once an absent shim is reported rather than skipped, a deliberate opt-out and
# an accidental deletion look identical to the instrument. Without this file it
# must report both or neither, and reporting neither is what the previous
# behaviour chose — the failure that let five repositories carry unmarked inlined
# copies unreported.
#
# An opt-out is reported AS an opt-out, with its reason, and does not count as a
# finding. It is never silence: a hook nobody binds on purpose is still a fact
# about the fleet, and the next migration that re-adds the registration should
# meet the reason before it meets the file.
#
# THE REASON BELONGS WITH THE PROJECT, NOT ONLY HERE. This line is an index. The
# argument lives in the project's own ADR, because a rationale kept only in
# another repository's declaration is one `git clone` away from being lost — and
# the one live instance below had already been manually reverted about three
# times when it was carried as a comment inside the file it justified.
#
# Format: <repo> <hook> <reason>. One per line, blank lines and # ignored.

